-- title:
--   Toric and finite parts of J_H(M)[m] multiply to #J_H(M)[m]
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, and let $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ be a subgroup containing the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$, i.e. every unit $u$ with `ZMod.unitsMap` image $1$ lies in $H$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $p$ in the sense that $p$ is a non-unit of $A$, with residue field algebraically closed of characteristic $p$. Let $\Lambda$ be level data at $A$ (a structure morphism $\sigma_A : \operatorname{Spec} A \to$ `base p` restricting to the generic point, a scheme with relative group law over `base p`, and bijections of its generic and special sections with $J_H(M/p)$-points at the induced level subgroup and with $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the special function field), and let $O$ be a Néron object at $p$ for these data: a smooth, separated, quasi-compact, surjective group scheme $G \to$ `base p` of locally finite type with preconnected fibres, commutative relative group law, an additive Galois-equivariant bijection `pts` of $J_H(M)$ with the sections over the generic point, Hecke endomorphisms compatible with `pts`, flat surjective multiplication-by-$n$ maps, and the further data recorded in the structure. Let $m \ge 1$ be coprime to $p$. Here $J_H(M)$ is the degree-zero divisor class group $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of `xHFunctionFieldBar M H`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the function field of $X_H(M)$. Then: the toric subgroup `O.toricPts m`, generated by the range of the family `O.toricPoint m`, and the finite subgroup `O.finPts m`, generated by those classes $x$ which are $m$-torsion and whose associated section `O.pts x` extends over the place $A$ along $\Lambda.\sigma_A$, are both contained in the $m$-torsion subgroup $\mathrm{Pic}^0[m]$ (the $\mathbb{Z}$-torsion submodule for $m$), and their cardinalities satisfy $\#\,(\mathtt{toricPts}\ m) \cdot \#\,(\mathtt{finPts}\ m) = \#\,\mathrm{Pic}^0[m]$.
--
--   This is the splitting of the prime-to-$p$ torsion of $J_H(M)$ at a prime $p$ exactly dividing the level into a toric part, coming from the character lattice of the supersingular crossings on the special fibre, and a part extending to the Néron model, the two orders being $m^t$ and $m^{2g-t}$ in classical terms. It feeds the analysis of the $m$-torsion used in the level-lowering argument at $p \parallel M$, and is cited by [`ModularCurve.JHNeronObjectAtP.exists_forall_mem_toricPts_exists_smul_sub_eq_of_coprime_of_abelJacobiPin_of_atkinLehner`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JHNeronObjectAtP.exists_forall_mem_toricPts_exists_smul_sub_eq_of_coprime_of_abelJacobiPin_of_atkinLehner).
